# Production vendor/ IS committed for GitHub-based deploys (Deployer
# for Git ships the zip from the repo, doesn't run composer
# server-side).
#
# composer.lock IS COMMITTED as of #191. It used to be ignored, which let
# the committed tree and CI's fresh resolution drift apart silently — 272
# vendor files, 10 production packages, including brick/math 0.17.1 vs
# 1.0.0. CI now runs `composer install`, so the lock is the single pinned
# production set and committed == resolved by construction. Regenerate it
# with `composer update`, deliberately, as its own reviewable change.
#
# Dev-only paths below stay gitignored so restoring the dev tools locally
# does not dirty git status. ⚠ That is only HALF true and always was: a
# plain `composer install` (with dev) also rewrites the TRACKED
# vendor/composer/autoload_*.php pair into its dev flavour, because the
# committed autoloader is generated --no-dev. See
# docs/running-phpstan-locally.md.
/vendor/bin/
/vendor/phpstan/
/vendor/php-stubs/
/vendor/szepeviktor/
.phpunit.result.cache
.phpunit.cache/
*.log
# Dev-only test deps (PHPUnit tree) — restored via composer install, not shipped.
/vendor/phpunit/
/vendor/myclabs/
/vendor/nikic/
/vendor/phar-io/
/vendor/sebastian/
/vendor/staabm/
/vendor/theseer/

# Dev-only WP-CLI tree — pulled by the `wp-cli/wp-cli` require-dev that lets
# CosmwasmCliSynopsisTest run the REAL synopsis parser instead of a replica.
# `/vendor/wp-cli/` covers all four packages composer installs under it:
# wp-cli/wp-cli, wp-cli/php-cli-tools, wp-cli/mustache and
# wp-cli/mustangostang-spyc — there is no top-level /vendor/mustache/ or
# /vendor/mustangostang/ to ignore.
#
# symfony/finder is listed individually and NOT as /vendor/symfony/, because
# three symfony packages (deprecation-contracts, polyfill-mbstring,
# polyfill-php82) are COMMITTED production dependencies; a blanket rule would
# hide them from git and they would stop shipping.
/vendor/wp-cli/
/vendor/symfony/finder/

# Local-only agent instructions (not shared via git — see Tia/Phillip agreement 2026-07-08)
CLAUDE.md
